  "sampling": "Official: round-robin over split.json train ids in file order, one row per family per turn. Within a family, bases stay in collect_bases order (test index, then loo index). Each base is expanded by color table outer (ident, perm1, perm2, perm3) and geometry inner (ident, rot90, rot180, rot270, flipud, fliplr) before the next base repeats that 24-step cycle. iter_augmented()'s ident/perm1 front prefix is not used. Cap 12000. ARC-GEN: V2 import order after '# V2 Tasks', minus diag and holdout via exclude_arcgen_families. Each allowed family receives one kept instance before any family receives a second. An instance is four generate() calls, slots 0-2 demos and slot 3 query, seeded by sha256 of '20260930:'+task_id+':'+instance+':'+slot (first 8 bytes, little-endian) into random.seed. A rejected slot appends ':'+attempt and is retried up to 20 times. A generate() call that does not return within 10 seconds is a failed attempt (generate_timeout), not a stored grid. Kept bases are then expanded across the same 24-step cycle, one augmentation at a time across bases, until 18000 rows. Neither side borrows rows from the other.",
